research/audit/wave11-refuter-tasks/fs-substitution-holds-for-every-integrable-integrand.md-90-[L5] First fundamental theorem: for $u$ integrable on $[p,q]$ and continuous at every point, $x \mapsto \int_p^x u$ is differentiable with derivative $u$ ([[thm-ftc-first-part]], [[def-the-integral-function]], [[thm-additivity-over-subintervals]], [[def-oriented-integral]]).
research/audit/wave11-refuter-tasks/fs-substitution-holds-for-every-integrable-integrand.md-91-
research/audit/wave11-refuter-tasks/fs-substitution-holds-for-every-integrable-integrand.md-92-[L6] A continuous $w \ge 0$ on $[p,q]$ with $p<q$ and $\int_p^q w = 0$ vanishes identically ([[thm-nonnegative-continuous-with-zero-integral-vanishes]]).
research/audit/wave11-refuter-tasks/fs-substitution-holds-for-every-integrable-integrand.md-93-
research/audit/wave11-refuter-tasks/fs-substitution-holds-for-every-integrable-integrand.md:94:[L7] If $\kappa \le w \le \mu$ on $[p,q]$ with $w$ integrable then $\kappa(q-p) \le \int_p^q w \le \mu(q-p)$ ([[thm-monotonicity-of-the-integral]], [[lem-integral-elementary-bounds]]).
research/audit/wave11-refuter-tasks/fs-substitution-holds-for-every-integrable-integrand.md-95-
research/audit/wave11-refuter-tasks/fs-substitution-holds-for-every-integrable-integrand.md-96-[L8] The continuous image of a compact set is compact, and a compact subset of $\mathbb{R}$ is closed and bounded ([[thm-continuous-image-of-a-compact-set-r]], [[thm-heine-borel-characterisation-r]]).
research/audit/wave11-refuter-tasks/fs-substitution-holds-for-every-integrable-integrand.md-97-
research/audit/wave11-refuter-tasks/fs-substitution-holds-for-every-integrable-integrand.md-98-[L9] Lebesgue's criterion: a bounded function on $[p,q]$ is integrable if and only if its discontinuity set has measure zero; a set of content zero has measure zero ([[thm-lebesgue-criterion]], [[lem-content-zero-implies-null]], [[def-measure-zero-and-content-zero]], [[def-bounded-set]]).
