research/audit/wave11-refuter-tasks/fs-substitution-holds-for-every-integrable-integrand.md-5372-[L2] Continuity at $c$: for every real $\eta>0$ there is a real $\delta>0$ such that every $x \in [a,b]$ with $|x-c|<\delta$ satisfies $|f(x)-f(c)| < \eta$ ([[def-continuity-real]]).
research/audit/wave11-refuter-tasks/fs-substitution-holds-for-every-integrable-integrand.md-5373-
research/audit/wave11-refuter-tasks/fs-substitution-holds-for-every-integrable-integrand.md-5374-[L3] Additivity: for $a \le p \le q \le b$, $\int_a^b f = \int_a^p f + \int_p^q f + \int_q^b f$, the degenerate pieces being $0$ ([[thm-additivity-over-subintervals]], claim 3, [[def-oriented-integral]]).
research/audit/wave11-refuter-tasks/fs-substitution-holds-for-every-integrable-integrand.md-5375-
research/audit/wave11-refuter-tasks/fs-substitution-holds-for-every-integrable-integrand.md:5376:[L4] If $u \ge 0$ is integrable on $[p,q]$ with $p<q$ then $\int_p^q u \ge 0$; and if $u \ge \kappa$ there then $\int_p^q u \ge \kappa(q-p)$ ([[thm-monotonicity-of-the-integral]], [[lem-integral-elementary-bounds]]).
