research/audit/wave11-refuter-tasks/thm-second-mean-value-theorem-for-integrals.md-79-[L7] For a partition $P = (n,t)$ of $[a,b]$: $n \ge 1$, $t_0 = a$, $t_k = b$ for $k \ge n$, $\Delta_i = t_{i+1}-t_i > 0$ for $i<n$, $I_i = [t_i,t_{i+1}] \subseteq [a,b]$, and $U(f,P)-L(f,P) = \sum_{i<n}(M_i-m_i)\Delta_i$ with $m_i \le f(x) \le M_i$ for $x \in I_i$ ([[def-partition-and-refinement]], [[def-darboux-sums]]).
