research/audit/wave11-refuter-tasks/thm-second-mean-value-theorem-for-integrals.md-85-[L10] Absolute value and ordered-field arithmetic: $-c \le x \le c$ is equivalent to $|x| \le c$, multiplying an inequality by a positive real preserves it and by a negative real reverses it, the order is total and transitive, and a real that is $\le M + \eta$ for every real $\eta>0$ is $\le M$ ([[lem-of-abs-value]], [[def-abs-value]], [[def-ordered-field]], [[def-complete-ordered-field]]).
